# gstack writes its runtime state next to the project it is driving: a port,
# a pid, a token for its localhost endpoint, and network and audit logs of
# what it browsed. None of it belongs to this plugin, and the token in it was
# published for a day before anyone noticed. Ignored rather than remembered.
.gstack/

# An Arch package that wandered in here while testing. Not part of the plugin.
*.pkg.tar.zst
